======================================================================================
EXHAUSTIVE n<=6: Lemma A (mult>n/2 => integer), gap, rank(A)>=ceil(n/2)
======================================================================================
  n=3 : max-mult set observed = [1, 3]   (gap (floor(n/2),n) empty: True)
        Lemma A (unstable eigenvalue is an integer): True   unstable lambdas: {0: 6}
        min rank(A) over all T = 2   (>= ceil(n/2)=2 : True)
  n=4 : max-mult set observed = [1, 4]   (gap (floor(n/2),n) empty: True)
        Lemma A (unstable eigenvalue is an integer): True   unstable lambdas: {0: 24}
        min rank(A) over all T = 3   (>= ceil(n/2)=2 : True)
  n=5 : max-mult set observed = [1, 2, 5]   (gap (floor(n/2),n) empty: True)
        Lemma A (unstable eigenvalue is an integer): True   unstable lambdas: {0: 120}
        min rank(A) over all T = 4   (>= ceil(n/2)=3 : True)
  n=6 : max-mult set observed = [1, 2, 3, 6]   (gap (floor(n/2),n) empty: True)
        Lemma A (unstable eigenvalue is an integer): True   unstable lambdas: {0: 720}
        min rank(A) over all T = 5   (>= ceil(n/2)=3 : True)

======================================================================================
LEMMA B check (geometric mult <= floor(n/2) off Perron & -1/2), n=5,6 exhaustive
======================================================================================
  n=5 : max geometric mult off {Perron,-1/2} = 1  (<= floor(n/2)=2 : True)
  n=6 : max geometric mult off {Perron,-1/2} = 2  (<= floor(n/2)=3 : True)

======================================================================================
n=7 SAMPLE: is the gap (3.5, 7) empty? (no non-transitive with mult 4,5,6)
======================================================================================
  transitive char_A max |eig| = 0.000e+00 (should be ~0, nilpotent) -> mult 7
  over 400000 random n=7 tournaments, max multiplicity among NON-transitive = 4
  floor(n/2) = 3, so gap forbids mult in {4,5,6}; observed max non-transitive mult > 3
  (SAMPLE, not exhaustive: detection floor is 400000 random tournaments.)
